Date: Tue, 18 Aug 2026 02:28:31 -0700
Subject: [PATCH] Gallery: a real viewer; Apps & games: gone, WebUI included

Two launcher apps that did nothing.

Gallery. Upstream builds this app from an internal CIPD bundle
(enable_cros_media_app = is_chromeos && is_chrome_branded, resources/prod
via DEPS with checkout_src_internal); every other build gets a mock whose
zero state is a bare <img> with no src. That is the blank window on
colorburst, and we cannot fetch the internal bundle.

So the file that was the mock is now a small real viewer against the same
ClientApi the trusted context talks to: images with fit/zoom/rotate,
drag-pan and wheel zoom, video and audio with controls, RAW via the
delegate's preview extractor, prev/next across the handed-over file list
with a counter, and honest empty and error states. It carries its own
Vietnamese strings because the untrusted guest cannot reach the browser's
string bundle. It does not pretend to edit, annotate or render PDFs --
those are the internal parts -- and says so instead. The crash-reporting
hooks that phoned Google are replaced by console logging.

Verified in a VM against the running app: our element renders with its app
bar; a loaded PNG decodes and displays with the filename shown; zoom grows
the image; rotate applies rotate(90deg); fit restores; navigation controls
hide for a single file.

Apps & games. MallSystemAppDelegate::IsAppEnabled() now returns false, so
SystemWebAppManager never installs it -- no launcher icon, no shelf pin.
Upstream already does this for Flex via IsRevenBranding(), which colorburst
does not set.

That alone leaves chrome://mall reachable by URL, and the VM showed the
page immediately embedding https://discover.apps.chrome/ with the board,
OS and Chrome versions, hwid and locale in the query string. For a build
whose point is that it does not talk to Google, hiding the icon is not
enough, so the WebUI registration is dropped too and the host no longer
exists.

